<head>
  <title>DensRas: Raster densification</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
 <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 

  <p>This program changes the spatial resolution of a raster by interpolating
  its values. The program reads the documentation file and, if a NoData value is
  indicated, it is not considered in the interpolation process. Byte, (short)
  integer and real data types are supported.</p>

  <p>If it is densified exactly within the coordinates of the original raster (specifying the bounding box with the minimum and maximum X and Y coordinates) it must be taken into account that a simplification will be applied to the borders. Therefore, it is not
  convenient to connect by adjacency the result of the densification with
  another densification. In this case, it is better to have some extra area
  around the region considered as fully reliable. In addition, when
  densifying exactly the same coordinates than the original file, it is neither
  convenient to apply algorithms related to hydrological fluxes; if necessary,
  omit the most exterior concentric area:</p>

  <blockquote>
   <li> When using bilinear interpolation, eliminate a buffer of 1 pixel all
    around the image.</li>
	<li>When using bicubic interpolation eliminate a buffer of 2
    pixels all around the image.</li>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>RECOMMENDATIONS SUMMARY (where <a href="DensRas.htm">DensRas</a> program is indicated also applies to <a href="AdapRas.htm">AdapRas</a>AdapRas)
  <pre>
EXPANSION:  + Categorical map:   CanviRes [followed by the method in X. Pons' Ph D thesis]
            + Sensor image:      CanviRes for classification (not recommended)
                                 DensRas L, for visual analysis
            + DEM:               DensRas L

CONTRACTION:+ Categorical map:   CanviRes, M option
            + Sensor image:      CanviRes, C option for classification
                                 CanviRes, d or m option for visual analysis
            + DEM:               CanviRes, d or m option for median or mean heights
                                 DensRas L, for heights that prioritize central values in the resulting cell
</pre><hr/>

